<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        Unique identity for a dispatch claim.

        A claim used to be identified by the timestamp it wrote (started_at for an IDLE claim,
        retry_eligible_at for a retry claim), which the activation, skip and failure guards matched for
        exact equality. started_at and retry_eligible_at are legacy DATETIME columns holding whole seconds,
        so that identity is only second-resolution: a content update that requeues a unit between two pull
        claims taken in the same second leaves both claims carrying the same marker, and the earlier claim's
        activation then matches the newer claim and attaches its stale job token and content fingerprint.
        Pull claims are not serialized by the cluster-wide dispatch lock, so nothing else prevents it.

        claim_token gives every claim its own identity instead. It is written afresh by each claim, matched
        by every guard that commits a claim's outcome, and cleared by every path that releases a claim, so a
        superseded claim can never match a newer one however close together they were taken.

        Nullable, no data migration: rows are unclaimed most of the time, and a claim taken before this
        column existed simply has none. Those in-flight claims cannot be matched by the new guards and are
        released by the abandoned-claim sweep (IDLE) or their lapsing lease (retry), which is the same
        recovery any interrupted claim already relies on.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260922160000-1" author="artemis">
        <addColumn tableName="lecture_unit_processing_state">
            <column name="claim_token" type="VARCHAR(36)"/>
        </addColumn>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
